cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Aether: a production platform for masked diffusion language models"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Amey
    family-names: Gupta
    affiliation: "BITS Pilani"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ameyg910/aether"
url: "https://ameyg910.github.io/aether/"
abstract: >-
  Aether is an end-to-end platform for masked (absorbing-state) diffusion
  language models, covering data preparation, distributed training, evaluation,
  inference serving with dynamic batching, and Kubernetes deployment with
  autoscaling and observability.
keywords:
  - diffusion models
  - language models
  - MLOps
  - distributed training
  - inference serving
license: Apache-2.0
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-07-31"
references:
  - type: article
    title: "Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models"
    authors:
      - family-names: Sahoo
        given-names: Subham
    year: 2024
    notes: "MDLM/SUBS formulation implemented here; see docs/adr/0001."
  - type: article
    title: "Structured Denoising Diffusion Models in Discrete State-Spaces"
    authors:
      - family-names: Austin
        given-names: Jacob
    year: 2021
    notes: "D3PM; the absorbing-state process."
